  {
   "id": "ID_2024_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_FONT_OF_INSPIRATION",
   "name": "Font of Inspiration",
   "type": "Class Feature",
   "source": "SRD 5.2.1",
   "ruleset": "dnd2024",
   "description": "<p>You now regain all your expended uses of Bardic Inspiration when you finish a Short or Long Rest.</p>\n<p>In addition, you can expend a spell slot (no action required) to regain one expended use of Bardic Inspiration.</p>",
   "rules": [
    {
     "kind": "resource_regain",
     "resource": "bardic inspiration",
     "on": [
      "short_rest",
      "long_rest"
     ]
    },
    {
     "kind": "resource_regain",
     "resource": "bardic inspiration",
     "by": "expend a spell slot",
     "amount": 1
    }
   ],
   "data": {
    "class": "Bard",
    "level": 5
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ID_2024_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_COUNTERCHARM",
   "name": "Countercharm",
   "type": "Class Feature",
   "source": "SRD 5.2.1",
   "ruleset": "dnd2024",
   "description": "<p>You can use musical notes or words of power to disrupt mind-influencing effects. If you or a creature within 30 feet of you fails a saving throw against an effect that applies the Charmed or Frightened condition, you can take a Reaction to cause the save to be rerolled, and the new roll has Advantage.</p>",
   "data": {
    "class": "Bard",
    "level": 7
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ID_2024_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_MAGICAL_SECRETS",
   "name": "Magical Secrets",
   "type": "Class Feature",
   "source": "SRD 5.2.1",
   "ruleset": "dnd2024",
   "description": "<p>You’ve learned secrets from various magical traditions. Whenever you reach a Bard level (including this level) and the Prepared Spells number in the Bard Features table increases, you can choose any of your new prepared spells from the Bard, Cleric, Druid, and Wizard spell lists, and the chosen spells count as Bard spells for you (see a class’s section for its spell list). In addition, whenever you replace a spell prepared for this class, you can replace it with a spell from those lists.</p>",
   "rules": [
    {
     "kind": "spell_list_extend",
     "spell_class": "Bard",
     "lists": [
      "Cleric",
      "Druid",
      "Wizard"
     ],
     "for_prepared": true
    }
   ],
   "data": {
    "class": "Bard",
    "level": 10
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ID_2024_CLASS_FEATURE_BARD_SUPERIOR_INSPIRATION",
   "name": "Superior Inspiration",
   "type": "Class Feature",
   "source": "SRD 5.2.1",
   "ruleset": "dnd2024",
   "description": "<p>When you roll Initiative, you regain expended uses of Bardic Inspiration until you have two if you have fewer than that.</p>",
   "rules": [
    {
     "kind": "resource_regain",
     "resource": "bardic inspiration",
     "on": [
      "initiative"
     ],
     "up_to": 2
    }
   ],
   "data": {
    "class": "Bard",
    "level": 18
   }
  },
  {
